WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.058 --> 00:00:11.799
Detective Fix had been watching Mr.

2
00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:14.081
Fogg and Aouda since their arrival at the quay.

3
00:00:15.221 --> 00:00:16.022
He approached Mr.

4
00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:21.405
Fogg innocently and asked, "Were you not, like me sir, a passenger on the Rangoon?"

5
00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:23.807
"I was," replied Mr.

6
00:00:23.847 --> 00:00:25.968
Fogg. "But we have not been introduced."

7
00:00:25.988 --> 00:00:28.510
"Pardon me," said Fix.

8
00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.092
"I thought I would find your servant here."

9
00:00:31.796 --> 00:00:33.036
"Do you know where he is, sir?"

10
00:00:33.377 --> 00:00:34.597
asked Aouda anxiously.

11
00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:38.158
"What?" responded Fix, pretending to be surprised.

12
00:00:38.178 --> 00:00:39.938
"He is not with you?"

13
00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:42.099
"No," said Aouda.

14
00:00:42.119 --> 00:00:44.260
"We have not seen him since yesterday.

15
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.800
Could he have boarded the Carnatic without us?"

16
00:00:47.961 --> 00:00:50.882
"Did you intend on sailing on the Carnatic as well?"

17
00:00:51.302 --> 00:00:51.902
asked Fix.

18
00:00:51.922 --> 00:00:55.723
"I am very disappointed, but I have missed it also.

19
00:00:56.463 --> 00:00:59.004
Apparently there won't be another steamer for a week."

20
00:00:59.712 --> 00:01:03.514
"But there are other vessels in the harbor besides the Carnatic," replied Mr.

21
00:01:03.554 --> 00:01:04.535
Fogg with confidence.

22
00:01:05.835 --> 00:01:07.996
He held out his arm to Aouda, and they walked off.

23
00:01:08.437 --> 00:01:09.377
Fix grew alarmed.

24
00:01:11.518 --> 00:01:13.760
He had not expected Fogg to be so determined.

25
00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.821
For three hours Fix watched Mr.

26
00:01:16.841 --> 00:01:19.202
Fogg and Aouda wander the docks looking for a ship.

27
00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:21.083
He began to hope again.

28
00:01:22.424 --> 00:01:23.725
Then a sailor approached Mr.

29
00:01:23.765 --> 00:01:26.506
Fogg. "Is Your Honor looking for a boat?"

30
00:01:26.806 --> 00:01:27.287
he asked.

31
00:01:27.307 --> 00:01:29.448
"Do you have a boat ready to sail?"

32
00:01:29.872 --> 00:01:30.453
asked Mr.

33
00:01:30.493 --> 00:01:33.195
Fogg. "Yes, your honor," replied the sailor.

34
00:01:33.215 --> 00:01:34.616
"The best in the harbor."

35
00:01:35.337 --> 00:01:37.398
"Will you agree to take me to Yokohama?"

36
00:01:37.739 --> 00:01:38.319
asked Mr.

37
00:01:38.359 --> 00:01:40.361
Fogg. "Is Your Honor joking?"

38
00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:41.382
said the sailor.

39
00:01:41.402 --> 00:01:42.843
"It is impossible."

40
00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:49.648
"I have missed the Carnatic, and I must get to Yokohama by November 14," said Fogg.

41
00:01:49.668 --> 00:01:55.793
"I offer you one-hundred pounds per day and an additional two- hundred pounds if I reach Yokohama in

42
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:57.695
time." "Are you in earnest?"

43
00:01:58.155 --> 00:01:58.896
asked the sailor.

44
00:01:59.816 --> 00:02:01.397
"Very much so," said Mr.

45
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:05.800
Fogg. The sailor walked away a little distance and gazed out to sea.

46
00:02:06.961 --> 00:02:11.784
He was struggling between the temptation of such a large sum and the danger of traveling so far.

47
00:02:12.604 --> 00:02:13.825
Fix watched in suspense.

48
00:02:14.746 --> 00:02:18.668
Mr. Fogg turned to Aouda and asked her, "You would not be afraid, would you, madam?"

49
00:02:19.769 --> 00:02:20.590
"Not with you, Mr.

50
00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.750
Fogg," she answered.

51
00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:22.971
"Well, sailor?"

52
00:02:23.291 --> 00:02:23.732
said Mr.

53
00:02:23.772 --> 00:02:30.285
Fogg. "Your Honor, I could not risk myself, my men, or my little boat on such a long

54
00:02:30.325 --> 00:02:31.385
voyage at this time of year.

55
00:02:32.406 --> 00:02:35.827
Besides, we would not reach Yokohama in time," answered the sailor.

56
00:02:36.747 --> 00:02:38.087
Fix breathed more freely.

57
00:02:38.107 --> 00:02:42.108
"But," added the sailor, "it might be arranged another way."

58
00:02:43.649 --> 00:02:44.589
Fix held his breath.

59
00:02:44.609 --> 00:02:47.010
"How?" asked Mr.

60
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.310
Fogg. "By going to Shanghai," said the sailor.

61
00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:56.404
"Sir, I must take the American steamer at Yokohama, not at Shanghai," said Mr.

62
00:02:56.424 --> 00:03:00.487
Fogg. "It isn't necessary to go as far as Yokohama," said the sailor.

63
00:03:00.507 --> 00:03:03.888
"The San Francisco steamer does not start from Yokohama.

64
00:03:04.569 --> 00:03:05.749
It begins at Shanghai."

65
00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:07.410
"You are sure of that?"

66
00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:08.311
asked Mr.

67
00:03:08.351 --> 00:03:10.052
Fogg. "Perfectly!"

68
00:03:10.392 --> 00:03:11.232
replied the sailor.

69
00:03:11.252 --> 00:03:13.854
"And when does the boat leave Shanghai?"

70
00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:14.794
asked Fogg.

71
00:03:14.814 --> 00:03:18.396
"On November 11, at seven in the evening," said the sailor.

72
00:03:18.416 --> 00:03:20.137
"We have four days before us."

73
00:03:20.157 --> 00:03:21.838
"And when can we leave?"

74
00:03:22.238 --> 00:03:22.798
asked Mr.

75
00:03:22.838 --> 00:03:25.500
Fogg. "In an hour," the sailor replied.

76
00:03:26.548 --> 00:03:27.208
"It is a deal.

77
00:03:27.729 --> 00:03:28.949
Are you the master of the boat?"

78
00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:30.010
asked Fogg.

79
00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.031
"Yes," replied the sailor.

80
00:03:32.051 --> 00:03:34.832
"My name is John Bunsby, captain of the Tankadere."

81
00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:38.333
The two men sealed their deal and Mr.

82
00:03:38.374 --> 00:03:40.675
Fogg gave John Bunsby a sum of money in advance.

83
00:03:41.555 --> 00:03:42.816
"But poor Passepartout!"

84
00:03:43.176 --> 00:03:43.796
urged Aouda.

85
00:03:43.816 --> 00:03:45.677
"We can't leave him behind."

86
00:03:45.697 --> 00:03:49.259
"I will do all I can to find him," replied Mr.

87
00:03:49.279 --> 00:03:52.836
Fogg. Before heading out in search of Passepartout, Mr.

88
00:03:52.856 --> 00:03:54.098
Fogg offered to let Mr.

89
00:03:54.118 --> 00:03:56.400
Fix join them as a passenger on the Tankadere.

90
00:03:57.121 --> 00:03:58.923
Mr. Fix could do nothing but accept.

91
00:03:59.724 --> 00:04:02.446
In a nervous state, Fix boarded the Tankadere while Mr.

92
00:04:02.486 --> 00:04:04.909
Fogg and Aouda went to the local police station.

93
00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.813
Phileas Fogg left Passepartout's description with the police.

94
00:04:09.674 --> 00:04:12.397
He also left a sum of money to be spent in search of him.

95
00:04:14.058 --> 00:04:15.380
By now it was three o'clock.

96
00:04:16.428 --> 00:04:20.909
They had stopped at the hotel, picked up their luggage, and arrived at the Tankadere just as the

97
00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:22.870
last of the boat's supplies were being stored.

98
00:04:25.291 --> 00:04:27.871
The Tankadere was a little boat with two tall masts.

99
00:04:28.852 --> 00:04:33.253
Its deck was as white as ivory, and all its brass fittings were polished to a shine.

100
00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:38.255
The boat was as graceful as a racing yacht, and it was obvious the captain took pride in

101
00:04:38.335 --> 00:04:40.375
it. Mr.

102
00:04:40.415 --> 00:04:42.676
Fogg and Aouda found Fix already on board.

103
00:04:43.584 --> 00:04:46.445
Below deck was a square cabin with cots set in the walls.

104
00:04:47.605 --> 00:04:50.006
In the center was a table with a swinging lamp above.

105
00:04:51.106 --> 00:04:52.987
The accommodations were small but neat.

106
00:04:53.007 --> 00:04:56.948
"I am sorry to have nothing better to offer you," said Mr.

107
00:04:56.988 --> 00:04:59.228
Fogg to Fix, who bowed without responding.

108
00:05:00.309 --> 00:05:03.530
The detective felt humiliated for relying on the kindness of Mr.

109
00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:08.931
Fogg. "He may be a rascal," thought Fix, "but he is a polite one!"

110
00:05:09.951 --> 00:05:12.052
The sails were raised at ten minutes past three.

111
00:05:12.852 --> 00:05:17.415
Mr. Fogg and Aouda, who were seated on the deck, cast a last glance at the quay in

112
00:05:17.435 --> 00:05:19.116
the hopes of seeing Passepartout.

113
00:05:19.897 --> 00:05:21.938
The Frenchman, however, did not appear.

114
00:05:26.301 --> 00:05:30.444
You can imagine my disappointment when I found out that I had missed seeing Shanghai with Mr.

115
00:05:30.484 --> 00:05:31.144
Fogg and Aouda.

116
00:05:31.965 --> 00:05:33.246
Although considering the way Mr.

117
00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:35.907
Fogg travels, I guess I wouldn't have seen much of it anyway.

118
00:05:37.048 --> 00:05:37.949
Oh, how unfortunate!

119
00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.512
For many years Shanghai was a small Chinese port.

120
00:05:43.244 --> 00:05:46.687
Before the nineteenth century, Asian countries had little to do with the West.

121
00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:49.148
They preferred to trade with each other.

122
00:05:50.089 --> 00:05:54.592
But during the first part of this century, Asian countries felt more pressure to begin trading with the

123
00:05:54.632 --> 00:06:00.757
West. When countries like China and Japan refused, European and American armies sometimes attacked them!

124
00:06:01.977 --> 00:06:05.680
As if attacking a country would make it more willing to do business with you!

125
00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.964
In 1839 Britain and China went to war over the opium trade, and three years later, Britain won.

126
00:06:11.888 --> 00:06:15.294
As a result, the port of Shanghai was opened to international trade.

127
00:06:16.396 --> 00:06:20.042
Many foreigners settled there, mainly British, French, and American citizens.
